1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,471
You have a SonarQube server. But it is empty. How do your own code and the server meet?

2
00:00:06,021 --> 00:00:06,786
With a scan.

3
00:00:06,786 --> 00:00:08,954
One Maven command reads your code,

4
00:00:08,954 --> 00:00:09,528
tests it,

5
00:00:09,528 --> 00:00:11,759
and sends the report to the server.

6
00:00:12,309 --> 00:00:17,280
But the server will not accept it from just anyone. You need a token, and a project key.

7
00:00:17,830 --> 00:00:22,822
Today we run a real scan on the CloudCart project, and watch it appear in the browser.

8
00:00:24,372 --> 00:00:25,801
Here is what to expect.

9
00:00:26,351 --> 00:00:28,549
One: how a scan works, in three parts.

10
00:00:29,099 --> 00:00:34,155
Two: the three things a scan needs. A token, a project key, and the server address.

11
00:00:34,705 --> 00:00:35,967
Three: a live scan.

12
00:00:35,967 --> 00:00:37,163
We create a token,

13
00:00:37,163 --> 00:00:38,625
run the Maven command,

14
00:00:38,625 --> 00:00:39,688
read the output,

15
00:00:39,688 --> 00:00:41,083
and open the results.

16
00:00:41,633 --> 00:00:44,257
Four: the common mistakes, and the lab files.

17
00:00:44,807 --> 00:00:47,858
This is objective three of the SonarQube domain.

18
00:00:49,408 --> 00:00:50,517
How a scan works.

19
00:00:51,067 --> 00:00:51,446
First,

20
00:00:51,446 --> 00:00:54,289
Maven builds your project and runs the tests.

21
00:00:54,289 --> 00:00:56,374
It also writes a coverage report,

22
00:00:56,374 --> 00:00:57,574
if you ask for one.

23
00:00:58,124 --> 00:00:58,546
Second,

24
00:00:58,546 --> 00:01:00,715
the scanner reads your source files,

25
00:01:00,715 --> 00:01:01,859
and looks for bugs,

26
00:01:01,859 --> 00:01:03,607
smells and security problems.

27
00:01:04,157 --> 00:01:08,381
Third, it packs the results into one report, and uploads it to the server.

28
00:01:08,931 --> 00:01:11,204
The server then processes that report.

29
00:01:11,204 --> 00:01:12,580
It takes a few seconds.

30
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:15,032
Then the project shows up in the browser.

31
00:01:15,582 --> 00:01:20,809
Important: the scanner does the heavy work. The server only stores and shows the results.

32
00:01:22,359 --> 00:01:24,620
Next, the three things every scan needs.

33
00:01:25,170 --> 00:01:29,266
The server address. For us, that is localhost, port nine thousand.

34
00:01:29,816 --> 00:01:30,876
The project key.

35
00:01:30,876 --> 00:01:33,658
A short name that is unique on the server.

36
00:01:33,658 --> 00:01:34,916
Ours is CloudCart.

37
00:01:34,916 --> 00:01:36,837
Scan again with the same key,

38
00:01:36,837 --> 00:01:39,950
and you add a new analysis to the same project.

39
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:41,402
And the token.

40
00:01:41,402 --> 00:01:43,078
It proves who is scanning.

41
00:01:43,078 --> 00:01:44,368
It is a long secret,

42
00:01:44,368 --> 00:01:46,366
like a password made for tools.

43
00:01:46,916 --> 00:01:49,784
Never type the token into a file that you share.

44
00:01:49,784 --> 00:01:51,874
Pass it as an environment variable.

45
00:01:51,874 --> 00:01:53,188
We will do that today.

46
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:57,962
And use the full plugin name, with its group. Then Maven always finds it.

47
00:01:59,512 --> 00:02:00,352
Let us scan.

48
00:02:00,352 --> 00:02:01,962
We start in a terminal,

49
00:02:01,962 --> 00:02:04,272
in the CloudCart project folder.

50
00:02:04,272 --> 00:02:05,742
We run ls to see it.

51
00:02:05,742 --> 00:02:07,492
There is a pom.xml,

52
00:02:07,492 --> 00:02:09,033
and the source folder.

53
00:02:09,033 --> 00:02:11,203
That is a normal Maven project.

54
00:02:11,753 --> 00:02:13,719
Does it have any Sonar settings?

55
00:02:13,719 --> 00:02:15,994
We search the pom for the word sonar,

56
00:02:15,994 --> 00:02:17,346
and count the matches.

57
00:02:17,346 --> 00:02:17,653
Zero.

58
00:02:17,653 --> 00:02:20,665
So you do not have to change your project at all.

59
00:02:20,665 --> 00:02:23,123
The scan is added from the command line.

60
00:02:23,673 --> 00:02:24,748
Now the browser.

61
00:02:24,748 --> 00:02:26,024
We open localhost,

62
00:02:26,024 --> 00:02:27,300
port nine thousand,

63
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:29,583
and log in with the admin account.

64
00:02:29,583 --> 00:02:32,604
The Projects page offers to create a project,

65
00:02:32,604 --> 00:02:35,492
because the server has never seen our code.

66
00:02:42,042 --> 00:02:42,429
First,

67
00:02:42,429 --> 00:02:43,075
the token.

68
00:02:43,075 --> 00:02:44,688
We open the account menu,

69
00:02:44,688 --> 00:02:45,334
top right,

70
00:02:45,334 --> 00:02:46,754
and choose My Account.

71
00:02:46,754 --> 00:02:48,174
Then the Security tab.

72
00:02:48,174 --> 00:02:49,658
Here you create tokens.

73
00:02:56,208 --> 00:02:58,886
We give the token a name: CloudCart scan.

74
00:02:58,886 --> 00:03:00,863
We choose the type: user token.

75
00:03:00,863 --> 00:03:01,819
It acts as you,

76
00:03:01,819 --> 00:03:02,776
so it can scan,

77
00:03:02,776 --> 00:03:04,306
and it can read results.

78
00:03:04,306 --> 00:03:04,689
Later,

79
00:03:04,689 --> 00:03:05,582
for pipelines,

80
00:03:05,582 --> 00:03:08,451
we will use a safer token that can only scan.

81
00:03:08,451 --> 00:03:09,918
Then we press Generate.

82
00:03:09,918 --> 00:03:11,767
The token is shown only once.

83
00:03:11,767 --> 00:03:13,361
A real token is a secret,

84
00:03:13,361 --> 00:03:15,784
so never show it in a video or a chat.

85
00:03:15,784 --> 00:03:17,314
This one is for the lab,

86
00:03:17,314 --> 00:03:19,419
and we will delete it afterwards.

87
00:03:21,469 --> 00:03:22,793
Back in the terminal.

88
00:03:22,793 --> 00:03:25,631
We keep the token in an environment variable,

89
00:03:25,631 --> 00:03:26,767
named Sonar token.

90
00:03:26,767 --> 00:03:29,164
The scanner reads that name by itself.

91
00:03:29,164 --> 00:03:30,614
We load it from a file,

92
00:03:30,614 --> 00:03:33,074
so that it never appears on the screen.

93
00:03:33,624 --> 00:03:34,514
Now the scan.

94
00:03:34,514 --> 00:03:35,747
One Maven command.

95
00:03:35,747 --> 00:03:38,213
Verify builds and tests the project.

96
00:03:38,213 --> 00:03:40,542
Then comes the Sonar Maven plugin,

97
00:03:40,542 --> 00:03:41,844
with its full name.

98
00:03:41,844 --> 00:03:43,487
We give the project key,

99
00:03:43,487 --> 00:03:45,063
and the server address.

100
00:03:45,063 --> 00:03:46,501
We filter the output,

101
00:03:46,501 --> 00:03:48,899
to show only the lines that matter.

102
00:03:49,449 --> 00:03:50,575
Watch the output.

103
00:03:50,575 --> 00:03:51,900
First the tests run,

104
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:52,828
and they pass.

105
00:03:52,828 --> 00:03:55,744
Then the Java sensor reads the source files.

106
00:03:55,744 --> 00:03:58,195
Then the analysis report is uploaded.

107
00:03:58,745 --> 00:04:00,652
It says: analysis successful.

108
00:04:00,652 --> 00:04:01,901
And: build success.

109
00:04:01,901 --> 00:04:04,005
Maven did all of this by itself,

110
00:04:04,005 --> 00:04:05,188
in under a minute.

111
00:04:27,738 --> 00:04:28,766
Now the browser.

112
00:04:28,766 --> 00:04:30,438
We open the Projects page,

113
00:04:30,438 --> 00:04:31,338
and reload it.

114
00:04:31,338 --> 00:04:32,559
Cloud cart is here.

115
00:04:32,559 --> 00:04:34,616
The server processed the report,

116
00:04:34,616 --> 00:04:37,509
and created the project from the project key.

117
00:04:42,059 --> 00:04:42,580
Open it.

118
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:43,947
This is the overview.

119
00:04:43,947 --> 00:04:45,835
At the top: the project name,

120
00:04:45,835 --> 00:04:47,268
and the lines of code.

121
00:04:47,268 --> 00:04:49,482
Then the project health dashboard.

122
00:04:49,482 --> 00:04:49,872
First,

123
00:04:49,872 --> 00:04:51,435
the quality gate status.

124
00:04:51,435 --> 00:04:52,412
It says Passed.

125
00:04:52,412 --> 00:04:52,737
Next,

126
00:04:52,737 --> 00:04:54,756
the number of issues: fourteen.

127
00:04:54,756 --> 00:04:55,928
Then duplications,

128
00:04:55,928 --> 00:04:56,774
and coverage.

129
00:04:56,774 --> 00:04:58,337
Coverage shows an error,

130
00:04:58,337 --> 00:05:01,527
because we did not ask for a coverage report yet.

131
00:05:01,527 --> 00:05:02,634
That is expected.

132
00:05:02,634 --> 00:05:04,523
We fix it in the next lesson.

133
00:05:05,973 --> 00:05:06,930
One more place.

134
00:05:06,930 --> 00:05:07,888
The Issues tab.

135
00:05:07,888 --> 00:05:10,761
Here are the real problems the scanner found,

136
00:05:10,761 --> 00:05:11,846
in our real code.

137
00:05:11,846 --> 00:05:12,868
Each has a file,

138
00:05:12,868 --> 00:05:13,762
a line number,

139
00:05:13,762 --> 00:05:14,719
and a severity.

140
00:05:18,269 --> 00:05:18,780
Finally,

141
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:20,504
prove it from the terminal.

142
00:05:20,504 --> 00:05:21,589
We run lab check.

143
00:05:21,589 --> 00:05:23,696
It checks four things: the token,

144
00:05:23,696 --> 00:05:24,462
the project,

145
00:05:24,462 --> 00:05:25,292
the analysis,

146
00:05:25,292 --> 00:05:26,696
and the lines of code.

147
00:05:28,246 --> 00:05:29,055
Four of four.

148
00:05:29,055 --> 00:05:31,047
The results are saved in a file.

149
00:05:31,047 --> 00:05:32,417
That is your evidence.

150
00:05:32,417 --> 00:05:33,164
Next lesson,

151
00:05:33,164 --> 00:05:35,094
we read these results properly.

152
00:05:36,644 --> 00:05:37,796
Five mistakes.

153
00:05:38,346 --> 00:05:43,743
One: leaving out the full plugin name. Maven says: no plugin found for prefix sonar.

154
00:05:44,293 --> 00:05:49,115
Two: a wrong or expired token. The scan fails with an authorization error.

155
00:05:49,665 --> 00:05:54,422
Three: a different project key each time. You get many projects, with no history.

156
00:05:54,972 --> 00:05:59,281
Four: saving the token in the pom, or in git. Anyone can then use it.

157
00:05:59,831 --> 00:06:04,461
Five: opening the dashboard too early. Wait for the server to finish processing.

158
00:06:06,011 --> 00:06:08,806
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

159
00:06:09,356 --> 00:06:10,820
One: the repository,

160
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:15,140
GitHub dot com slash it dash waves slash devops-ai,

161
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:17,484
in the folder academy slash lab.

162
00:06:18,034 --> 00:06:24,242
Two: the files, lab166.sh, and shortcuts166.sh.

163
00:06:24,792 --> 00:06:26,764
Three: load the short names,

164
00:06:26,764 --> 00:06:29,863
with source shortcuts166.sh.

165
00:06:29,863 --> 00:06:32,187
Then scan runs the Maven command,

166
00:06:32,187 --> 00:06:34,370
and lab check tests the result.

167
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:37,287
Four: set the variable Sonar token,

168
00:06:37,287 --> 00:06:38,505
to your own token.

169
00:06:38,505 --> 00:06:41,278
Never put it in a file in the repository.

170
00:06:41,828 --> 00:06:46,777
Five: your project can be any Maven project. Cloud cart is the one we use.

171
00:06:47,327 --> 00:06:48,970
The link is in the description.

172
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:51,395
Your turn.

173
00:06:51,945 --> 00:06:56,510
One: create a token in your own server, and keep it in an environment variable.

174
00:06:57,060 --> 00:07:00,985
Two: run the scan on a Maven project, with the full plugin name.

175
00:07:01,535 --> 00:07:05,951
Three: find your project on the Projects page, and open the Issues tab.

176
00:07:06,501 --> 00:07:09,019
Four: run lab check, and get four of four.

177
00:07:09,569 --> 00:07:12,982
Five: write down your project key and your server address.

178
00:07:13,532 --> 00:07:15,260
Pause the video, and do it now.

179
00:07:30,810 --> 00:07:31,685
Quick check.

180
00:07:32,235 --> 00:07:34,005
What are the three things a scan needs?

181
00:07:34,555 --> 00:07:37,158
Who does the heavy work, the scanner or the server?

182
00:07:37,708 --> 00:07:40,247
Why use an environment variable for the token?

183
00:07:40,797 --> 00:07:43,847
What happens if you scan with the same project key again?

184
00:07:44,397 --> 00:07:50,968
Objective covered: MC18, objective three. Run analysis for a Java Maven project.

185
00:07:51,518 --> 00:07:53,587
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

186
00:08:04,137 --> 00:08:07,743
Next: read the results, the issues, the metrics, and the coverage.

187
00:08:08,293 --> 00:08:11,621
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
